 "result_text": "Green now reports the `SyntaxError` when you name the module explicitly. I checked this with a small repro of your MWE. Running `python -m green tests.test_my` now shows `Failed to import \"tests.test_my\"` followed by the full `SyntaxError` traceback, where before it said \"No Tests Found\". I didn't run the project's test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `loadTarget` in `green/loader.py`. When loading a dotted name like `tests.test_my`, any exception from the import was caught and ignored. Nothing else matched the target, so green returned no tests.\n\nNow, if the import fails with something other than an `ImportError` (for example a `SyntaxError`) and no other lookup method finds tests, green reports a \"Failed to import\" error with the traceback. A target that can't be found at all still behaves as before.",
